      "id": 1,
      "text": "Montgomery Township was officially incorporated on February 21, 1798, emerging from the former Western Precinct of Somerset County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montgomery_Township%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The township’s name honors General Richard Montgomery, a Revolutionary War hero who fell fighting at Quebec in 1775.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montgomery_Township%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1875 the Delaware and Bound Brook Railroad opened depots at Skillman, Harlingen and Belle Mead, linking Montgomery to the regional rail network.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
